# Audit Logs in SkillUp How to request audit logs _Last updated: Jan 28, 2026, 10:13 AM (Last updated 3 months ago)_ Audit Logs provide a detailed record of organizational activity in SkillUp. Organizations can use audit logs to support governance, security monitoring, and compliance requirements. Audit logs capture key events performed within SkillUp, including: - User additions, removals, and role changes - Badge, certification, and assignment-related actions - Administrative configuration changes The information included in an audit log varies based on the request and the selected time period. # How to request audit logs To request audit logs, contact the SkillUp Support team at [skillup-support@hackerrank.com](mailto:skillup-support@hackerrank.com). **Note:** Only administrators can request audit logs for a SkillUp account. This restriction ensures that only authorized users can access organization-wide data. ## Sample template You can use the following template to request audit logs: ***Subject:*** *Request for SkillUp audit logs* \ *Hello SkillUp Support Team,* *I am requesting Audit Logs for our organization’s SkillUp account to support internal audit and compliance requirements.* *Request details:* - *Organization name: \[Your organization name\]* - *Requested time period: \[start date – end date\]* - *Relevant event types (if applicable): \[Categories of events to include. For example, user authentication, administrative actions, or assignments\]* *Thank you for your assistance.* *Kind regards,\ \[Your full name\]\ \[Your role/title\]\ \[Your organization\]\ \[Work email address\]* **Note:** If you have questions about audit logs or are unsure what information to provide, contact [skillup-support@hackerrank.com](mailto:skillup-support@hackerrank.com). \ \

